.Dd @PACKAGE_DATE@
.Dt GCLI-STATUS 1
.Os @PACKAGE_STRING@
.Sh NAME
.Nm gcli\ status
.Nd Work with TODO lists
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl l
.Op Fl n Ar number-of-items
.Nm
.Fl m Ar id
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is used to work with TODO lists of forges.
.Pp
When invoked without subcommand argumends, gcli will switch to interactive mode.
This interactive mode lets you select TODO list items,
operate on them by e.g. running actions or marking them as done.
The actions are documented in the respective manual pages of the item types.
If you, for example, select a TODO item that refers to an issue then you can invoke any action
that is documented in
.Xr gcli-issues 1
from within the prompt.
.Pp
All other invocations are non-interactive.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl n Ar number-of-items
Fetch at most
.Ar number-of-items
items and print them. If given a negative number, all notifications
are fetched. The default is 30.
.It Fl l , -list
List TODO list items non-interactively.
.It Fl m , -mark Ar id
Mark the TODO list item
.Ar id
as done.
This will cause the item to not appear on the TODO list anymore.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Print a TODO list for my-account:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gcli -a my-account status
.Ed
.Pp
Look through TODO list, select a merge request, view changes, approve it, merge and mark as done:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gcli status
NUMBER  REPO     TYPE          REASON
1       foo/bar  Pull Request  mentioned
Enter number, list or quit: 1
Enter action, done or quit: status
   NUMBER : 381
    TITLE : Foo bar baz
     HEAD : author:bork
     BASE : target:master
  CREATED : 1970-Jan-1 00:00:00
   AUTHOR : author
    STATE : open
   MERGED : no
MERGEABLE : yes
    DRAFT : no
ASSIGNEES : someone
REVIEWERS : none
Enter action, done or quit: diff
Enter action, done or quit: approve -y
Enter action, done or quit: merge
Enter action, done or quit: done
Enter number, list or quit: l
NUMBER  REPO  TYPE  REASON
Enter number, list or quit: q
.Ed
.Pp
The diff is viewed in a pager.
.Pp
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr gcli 1 ,
.Xr gcli-issues 1 ,
.Xr gcli-pulls 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Nico Sonack aka. herrhotzenplotz Aq Mt nsonack@herrhotzenplotz.de
and contributors.
.Sh BUGS
Please report bugs via E-Mail to
.Mt @PACKAGE_BUGREPORT@ .
.Pp
Alternatively you can report them on any of the forges linked at
.Lk @PACKAGE_URL@ .
However, the preferred and quickest method is to use the mailing
list.
